// Package startup is the platform entry/startup glue: the eventual home of the
// program entry points — the hosted C `main` (capturing argc/argv), the
// baremetal `_start`, and a C-library `_init` — selected per target by `#[build]`
// (design-ffi-export.md §3.3).  It is the startup counterpart to `rt`'s runtime
// *services* (alloc/refcount/exit): `rt` is services, `startup` is startup.  It
// is force-included in every hosted link (via cmd/bnc's ensureRuntimeDepsLoaded)
// so the entry glue can live here in Binate rather than in
// runtime/binate_runtime.c.
//
// It is deliberately ANODYNE for now — no exported surface, no functions, no
// init (it links only the same dead-strippable reflect descriptor + `__Package`
// accessor every package carries, and nothing more).
// It is introduced empty AHEAD of its content on purpose: the entry glue can
// only move here once a BUILDER that force-includes this package is pinned.  The
// current BUILDER does not force-include it, so a BUILDER-linked bnc does not
// contain it; real (needed) content would therefore be present in tree-built
// artifacts yet absent in BUILDER-built ones (e.g. gen1 itself).  Landing it
// empty, then re-pinning BUILDER, removes that asymmetry so a later bump can
// carry the real entry glue.  See plan-ffi-export-detailed.md Phase 6.
package "pkg/builtins/startup"
